==Strategy==
==='''Chapter 1'''===
Treat this stage as you would the original, except your Cats should have higher levels and more [[Treasure]]s. This time, Zory joins the monkey gang, so [[:Category:Anti-Zombie Cats|Anti-Zombies]] such as [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Polevaulter Cat]] can really help alongside the usual choices for this level. Additionally, the [[Ototo Corps|Holy Blast]] can be used to keep the Zories from burrowing, as they can prove troublesome if given the chance to burrow. Thankfully, this level does not have a lot of them added to the mix.

==='''Chapter 2'''===
[[Colossus Slayer]] and [[Behemoth Slayer]] units are naturally very useful against the respective enemies in this stage. A mix of generalists and specialists works well, though keep in mind that anti-Zombie cats are not necessary, as the Zory is a minor threat. Crowd controllers such as [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]] and [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercat]] are recommended as well. The Gory at the beginning can serve as free cash, especially if using a cat with Extra Money such as [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]] or Talented [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]]. Finally, long ranged and/or Weaken or Slow-immune cats are good.

==='''Chapter 3'''===
The buffed Aku Gories may seem inconvenient at first, but they can be handled relatively easily by [[Talents|Talented]] [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]. For other Gory types, [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]], [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] or any other high damage nuker will help take care of them. For meatshields, [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]] or [[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Shigong Cat]] are generally optimal, however Talented Awakened Bahamut Cat will usually shred the Gories in their entirety.

